> First Major Decision

You don't mention what is often the best way: switching between Mines and 
Sokoban as appropriate to circumstances.

If you're going to Minetown, you should at least explore down through DL5 
first, to check for shops.  If you then find a random altar, maybe 
Minetown isn't so urgent.  If the Oracle happens to be on DL5, you're 
already much closer to Sokoban than Minetown, so you might as well keep 
going.

On the other hand, if you're going to Sokoban, first pop into the Mines 
to grab a pickaxe and hopefully some mithril.  If the level is lit, and 
the next level is lit, keep going -- you can always turn back if it gets 
dangerous.

Anyway, this "major decision" shouldn't be made arbitrarily, as if 
picking red, black, or green at roulette, but based on circumstances that 
vary from game to game.

Reasons to enter/continue in the Mines:
- entrance on DL2
- you have a lamp to navigate dark levels
- you have a pickaxe to dig past dark levels (a little risky...)
- you have enough gold for one or more donations, taking into account 
possible XL gains on the way
- you've found items that make altar b/u/c especially important (magic 
lamp, special armors, lots of rings, etc.)

Reasons to avoid/leave the Mines:
- entrance on DL 4 (deeper is more dangerous)
- current mines level is dark (but see above)
- already have an altar in the main dungeon
- already found mithril, pickaxe, luckstone, etc
- dangerous monster appeared

Reasons to enter Sokoban first:
- Mines too risky or unrewarding
- Oracle on DL5-6
- you need food (?)

Reasons to avoid/leave Sokoban:
- you went to the Mines instead
- DL7 and still no Oracle (it can be as far as DL9)
- you messed up the boulders and now you need a pickaxe
- you already have BOH or reflection or both
- dangerous monster appeared, likely in the zoo




